# Task List Application - AI Assistant Guidelines

## Architecture Overview

### Dual File Structure
This application maintains **two versions of the same code**:
- `index.html` - Standalone single-file version with embedded JavaScript
- `js/app.js` - Modular version with separated JavaScript

**CRITICAL**: When modifying task/subtask logic, you MUST update BOTH files to keep them synchronized.

### Key Technologies
- Vanilla JavaScript (no frameworks)
- Local Storage for data persistence
- Web Workers for export generation
- Intersection Observer for lazy rendering
- CSS Custom Properties for theming

## Data Structure

### Task Object
```javascript
{
  id: number,                    // Unique timestamp-based ID
  title: string,                 // Task title
  content: string,               // Task description/notes
  completed: boolean,
  completedAt: string | null,    // ISO date string when completed
  archived: boolean,
  archivedAt: string | null,
  priority: 'low'|'medium'|'high',
  category: string,
  subtasks: Array<Subtask>,
  tags: Array<string>,
  dueDate: string | null,        // ISO date string
  createdAt: string,             // ISO date string
  updatedAt: string              // ISO date string
}
```

### Subtask Object
```javascript
{
  id: number,                    // Unique timestamp-based ID
  text: string,
  completed: boolean,
  completedAt: string | null     // ISO date string - CRITICAL for badges
}
```

## Critical Features to Preserve

### 1. Subtask Completion Badges
**Location**: Lines ~3079-3137 in both files

The `updateSubtaskDOM()` function is a **performance optimization** that updates individual subtasks without re-rendering the entire task list.

**MUST handle**:
- ✅ Creating completion date badge when subtask is checked
- ✅ Removing badge when subtask is unchecked
- ✅ Updating existing badge if date changes
- ✅ Proper positioning (before Edit/Delete buttons)

**Badge HTML Structure**:
```html
<span class="subtask-completed-date">✓ Dec 5</span>
```

**Date Format Consistency**:
```javascript
new Date(completedAt).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'short', day: 'numeric' })
```

### 2. Export System (Dual Format)

**Main Thread Export** (`formatTaskForExport()`):
- Used for general text export
- Located around lines 3515-3580
- Includes subtask completion dates
- Format: `✓ Subtask text (12/5/2024)`

**Web Worker Export**:
- Used for email-optimized export
- Embedded as string in `showExport()` function (~lines 3600-3700)
- Must match main thread export functionality
- Keeps UI responsive during large exports

**IMPORTANT**: Both export methods must be kept in sync for feature parity.

### 3. Performance Optimizations

#### Granular DOM Updates
- `updateSubtaskDOM()` - Update single subtask without re-render
- `updateSubtaskProgressDOM()` - Update progress bar only
- `updateTaskDOM()` - Update single task card

#### Lazy Rendering
- Intersection Observer monitors task cards
- Tasks render only when entering viewport
- Improves performance with 100+ tasks

#### Web Workers
- Export generation runs in worker thread
- UI remains responsive during export
- Worker code embedded as string (must escape backslashes)

### 4. Theme System

Uses CSS custom properties defined in `css/themes.css`:
```css
--bg-primary: background color
--text-primary: text color
--color-{category}: category colors
```

Theme applied via `data-theme` attribute on document.

## Common Modification Patterns

### Adding a Field to Tasks/Subtasks

1. Update data structure in both files
2. Update `renderTask()` or `renderSubtask()` to display the field
3. Update relevant DOM update functions (e.g., `updateSubtaskDOM()`)
4. Update both export functions (main thread + Web Worker)
5. Consider migration for existing localStorage data

### Modifying Export Formats

1. Update `formatTaskForExport()` in both files
2. Update Web Worker code string (remember `\\n` for newlines)
3. Test with various task configurations
4. Verify date formatting consistency

### Adding UI Controls

1. Add HTML elements to modal/form
2. Wire up event listeners
3. Update relevant functions to accept new parameters
4. Sync changes between `index.html` and `js/app.js`

## Code Location Reference

### Key Functions (approximate line numbers in js/app.js)

- `toggleSubtask()` - ~1816: Handles checkbox state and completedAt
- `updateSubtaskDOM()` - ~3079: Granular subtask updates WITH BADGES
- `renderSubtask()` - ~2681: Renders subtask HTML with badge
- `formatTaskForExport()` - ~3515: Main thread export formatter
- `showExport()` - ~3584: Export modal with Web Worker code
- `saveTasks()` - ~1574: Persists to localStorage
- `render()` - ~2467: Full task list render

### Export Modal HTML
- Located in `<div id="export-modal">` section
- Contains preview area and copy button
- Add new controls here for export options

## Testing Checklist

When making changes, verify:

- [ ] Changes applied to BOTH `index.html` AND `js/app.js`
- [ ] Subtask badges appear/disappear correctly on checkbox toggle
- [ ] Export includes all expected data
- [ ] Web Worker export matches main thread export
- [ ] Date formats are consistent across all displays
- [ ] No console errors
- [ ] localStorage data structure still valid
- [ ] Theme switching works
- [ ] Performance acceptable with 50+ tasks

## Debugging Tips

### Common Issues

**Badges not appearing**: Check `updateSubtaskDOM()` includes badge logic

**Export discrepancies**: Compare main thread vs Web Worker code

**Dates showing wrong**: Verify timezone handling and format strings

**Changes only work in one file**: Remember to sync both files!

### Console Logging

The app uses emoji prefixes for log categories:
- `✨` - Performance optimizations triggered
- `⚡` - Theme/UI changes
- `💾` - Storage operations

## Best Practices

1. **Always sync both files** when modifying task/subtask logic
2. **Preserve date format consistency** across all features
3. **Test with real data** from localStorage
4. **Consider performance** - use granular updates when possible
5. **Maintain export parity** between worker and main thread
6. **Document breaking changes** that affect stored data
7. **Test theme switching** after CSS/UI changes

